## 1. Single-file prototype

Save as `index.html` and open in a browser. Because the API supplies only “Thursday,” the prototype explicitly uses **Thursday, 18 June 2026 as a demo date**, not as a claim about real availability.

```html
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>PawPath · Book at Harbor Street</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      --primary: #7FD1AE;
      --ink: #1D2B33;
      --surface: #FFFFFF;
      --muted: #5E6B73;
      --radius: 12px;
    }

    * { box-sizing: border-box; }
    [hidden] { display: none !important; }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      background: var(--surface);
      color: var(--ink);
      font: 16px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif;
    }

    .app {
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 440px;
      margin: auto;
      padding: 16px;
    }

    h1 { margin: 4px 0; font-size: 26px; line-height: 1.25; }
    h2 { margin: 20px 0 12px; font-size: 21px; line-height: 1.3; }
    p { margin: 8px 0; }
    .brand { font-weight: 750; margin: 0; }
    .hint { color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; }
    .demo {
      border-left: 3px solid var(--ink);
      padding-left: 10px;
      margin: 14px 0;
    }

    .progress {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 6px;
      list-style: none;
      margin: 20px 0;
      padding: 0;
      font-size: 14px;
    }

    .progress li {
      border-bottom: 3px solid var(--muted);
      padding: 6px 0;
    }

    .progress li[aria-current="step"] {
      border-color: var(--ink);
      font-weight: 750;
    }

    fieldset { min-width: 0; border: 0; padding: 0; margin: 0; }
    legend { padding: 0; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: 650; }
    .choices { display: grid; gap: 10px; }

    .choice {
      display: flex;
      gap: 12px;
      align-items: flex-start;
      min-height: 64px;
      padding: 12px;
      border: 1px solid var(--muted);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    .choice:has(input:checked) {
      border: 2px solid var(--ink);
      padding: 11px;
    }

    .choice input {
      flex: 0 0 24px;
      width: 24px;
      height: 24px;
      margin: 2px 0 0;
      accent-color: var(--ink);
    }

    .choice span { min-width: 0; }
    .choice strong, .choice small { display: block; }
    .choice small { color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; }
    .unavailable { cursor: not-allowed; }
    .unavailable strong { color: var(--muted); }

    button {
      min-height: 48px;
      padding: 11px 14px;
      border: 2px solid var(--ink);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
      background: var(--primary);
      color: var(--ink); /* Deliberate accessible brand exception. */
      font: inherit;
      font-weight: 700;
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    button.secondary { background: var(--surface); }
    button:disabled {
      background: var(--surface);
      color: var(--muted);
      border-color: var(--muted);
      cursor: not-allowed;
    }

    :focus-visible {
      outline: 3px solid var(--ink);
      outline-offset: 3px;
    }

    .actions {
      display: flex;
      gap: 10px;
      margin-top: 20px;
    }

    .actions button { flex: 1; min-width: 0; }
    .card {
      margin-top: 20px;
      padding: 16px;
      border: 1px solid var(--muted);
      border-radius: var(--radius);
    }

    .card h2 { margin-top: 0; font-size: 18px; }
    dl { margin: 0; }
    .detail {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 72px minmax(0, 1fr);
      gap: 10px;
      padding: 8px 0;
    }
    dt { color: var(--muted); }
    dd { margin: 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
    #notice { font-weight: 650; }
    #notice:empty { display: none; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="app">
    <header>
      <p class="brand">PawPath</p>
      <h1>Book a visit</h1>
      <p>Harbor Street clinic</p>
      <p class="hint">12 Harbor Street, Example City</p>
      <p class="demo hint">
        Interactive demo only. No appointment is sent to the clinic.
        Thursday is the only supplied schedule.
      </p>
    </header>

    <main>
      <ol class="progress" aria-label="Booking progress">
        <li aria-current="step">1. Service</li>
        <li>2. Vet</li>
        <li>3. Time</li>
        <li>4. Review</li>
      </ol>

      <section aria-labelledby="step-title">
        <h2 id="step-title" tabindex="-1"></h2>
        <div id="content"></div>
        <p id="notice" role="alert"></p>
        <div class="actions">
          <button id="back" class="secondary" type="button">Back</button>
          <button id="next" type="button">Continue</button>
        </div>
      </section>

      <aside id="summary-wrap" class="card" aria-labelledby="summary-title">
        <h2 id="summary-title">Booking summary</h2>
        <div id="summary" role="status"
             aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></div>
      </aside>

      <noscript>
        <p>This interactive prototype requires JavaScript.</p>
      </noscript>
    </main>
  </div>

  <script>
    const services = {
      "Wellness exam": {
        minutes: 30, price: "$65", from: false,
        vets: ["Mary Major", "Richard Miles"], popular: true
      },
      "Vaccination visit": {
        minutes: 15, price: "$40", from: false,
        vets: ["Mary Major", "Richard Miles"], popular: true
      },
      "Dental cleaning": {
        minutes: 90, price: "from $280", from: true,
        vets: ["Mary Major"], popular: false
      },
      "Exotic pet check-up": {
        minutes: 45, price: "$85", from: false,
        vets: ["Mary Major"], popular: false
      }
    };

    const vets = {
      "Mary Major": { days: [2, 4, 6], schedule: "Tue, Thu, Sat" },
      "Richard Miles": {
        days: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6], schedule: "Mon–Sat"
      }
    };

    const rawSlots = [
      { vet: "Richard Miles", service: "Exotic pet check-up", start: "10:00" },
      { vet: "Mary Major", service: "Exotic pet check-up", start: "11:00" },
      { vet: "Mary Major", service: "Dental cleaning", start: "11:30" },
      { vet: "Richard Miles", service: "Wellness exam", start: "12:30" },
      { vet: "Richard Miles", service: "Wellness exam", start: "14:00" },
      { vet: "Mary Major", service: "Wellness exam", start: "16:45" }
    ];

    // Illustrative civil date only: the API did not provide one.
    const demoDate = "2026-06-18";
    const dateLabel = "Thursday, 18 June 2026 (demo)";
    const weekday = new Date(demoDate + "T00:00:00Z").getUTCDay();
    const clinicAddress = "12 Harbor Street, Example City";

    function minutes(time) {
      const match = /^([01]\d|2[0-3]):([0-5]\d)$/.exec(time);
      return match ? Number(match[1]) * 60 + Number(match[2]) : NaN;
    }

    function clock(value) {
      return String(Math.floor(value / 60)).padStart(2, "0") + ":" +
             String(value % 60).padStart(2, "0");
    }

    function bookable(slot) {
      const service = services[slot.service];
      const vet = vets[slot.vet];

      if (!service || !vet || !service.vets.includes(slot.vet)) return false;
      if (weekday === 0 || !vet.days.includes(weekday)) return false;

      const start = minutes(slot.start);
      const end = start + service.minutes;
      if (!Number.isFinite(start)) return false;

      // The entire appointment must fit inside one uninterrupted session.
      return (start >= 9 * 60 && end <= 12 * 60) ||
             (start >= 13 * 60 && end <= 17 * 60);
    }

    const validSlots = rawSlots.filter(bookable);
    const state = {
      step: 0, service: null, vet: "any", slot: null, done: false
    };

    const title = document.getElementById("step-title");
    const content = document.getElementById("content");
    const summary = document.getElementById("summary");
    const summaryWrap = document.getElementById("summary-wrap");
    const notice = document.getElementById("notice");
    const back = document.getElementById("back");
    const next = document.getElementById("next");
    const progress = document.querySelector(".progress");
    const headings = [
      "1. Choose a service",
      "2. Choose a vet",
      "3. Choose a time",
      "4. Review and confirm"
    ];

    function escapeHTML(value) {
      return String(value).replace(/[&<>"']/g, character => ({
        "&": "&amp;", "<": "&lt;", ">": "&gt;",
        '"': "&quot;", "'": "&#39;"
      })[character]);
    }

    function choice(name, value, label, detail, checked, disabled = false) {
      return `
        <label class="choice ${disabled ? "unavailable" : ""}">
          <input type="radio" name="${name}" value="${escapeHTML(value)}"
            ${checked ? "checked" : ""} ${disabled ? "disabled" : ""}
            required>
          <span>
            <strong>${escapeHTML(label)}</strong>
            <small>${escapeHTML(detail)}</small>
          </span>
        </label>`;
    }

    function matchingSlots() {
      return validSlots.filter(slot =>
        slot.service === state.service &&
        (state.vet === "any" || slot.vet === state.vet)
      );
    }

    function summaryHTML() {
      const service = services[state.service];
      let vetLabel = "Not selected";

      if (state.slot) {
        vetLabel = "Dr. " + state.slot.vet;
      } else if (service) {
        vetLabel = state.vet === "any"
          ? (service.vets.length === 1
             ? "Any eligible vet (Dr. Mary Major)"
             : "Any available vet — assigned when a time is chosen")
          : "Dr. " + state.vet;
      }

      const timeLabel = state.slot
        ? state.slot.start + "–" +
          clock(minutes(state.slot.start) + service.minutes)
        : "Not selected";

      const rows = [
        ["Service", state.service || "Not selected"],
        ["Price", service
          ? service.price + (service.from ? " — final estimate required" : "")
          : "Choose a service"],
        ["Vet", vetLabel],
        ["Date", dateLabel],
        ["Time", timeLabel],
        ["Clinic", "Harbor Street · " + clinicAddress]
      ];

      return "<dl>" + rows.map(([label, value]) =>
        `<div class="detail"><dt>${escapeHTML(label)}</dt>
         <dd>${escapeHTML(value)}</dd></div>`
      ).join("") + "</dl>";
    }

    function sync() {
      summary.innerHTML = summaryHTML();
      summaryWrap.hidden = state.step === 3 || state.done;
      progress.hidden = state.done;

      [...progress.children].forEach((item, index) => {
        if (!state.done && index === state.step) {
          item.setAttribute("aria-current", "step");
        } else {
          item.removeAttribute("aria-current");
        }
      });

      back.hidden = state.step === 0 || state.done;
      next.hidden = state.done;
      back.textContent = [
        "Back", "Back to service", "Back to vet", "Back to time"
      ][state.step];

      next.textContent = state.step === 3
        ? "Confirm booking" : "Continue";

      // No final dental estimate is supplied, so it cannot be confirmed.
      next.disabled = [
        !state.service,
        !state.vet,
        !state.slot,
        !state.slot || Boolean(services[state.service]?.from)
      ][state.step];
    }

    function render(moveFocus = false) {
      notice.textContent = "";
      title.textContent = state.done
        ? "Appointment confirmed (demo)" : headings[state.step];

      if (state.done) {
        content.innerHTML = `
          <p>Your simulated appointment details are below.
             No real appointment has been created.</p>
          ${summaryHTML()}
          <button class="secondary" type="button" id="restart">
            Book another visit
          </button>`;
      } else if (state.step === 0) {
        content.innerHTML = `
          <fieldset>
            <legend>Service (required)</legend>
            <div class="choices">
              ${Object.entries(services).map(([name, service]) =>
                choice("service", name, name,
                  `${service.minutes} min · ${service.price}` +
                  (service.popular ? " · Popular" : "") +
                  (service.from
                    ? " · Final estimate required before confirmation" : ""),
                  state.service === name)
              ).join("")}
            </div>
          </fieldset>`;
      } else if (state.step === 1) {
        const eligible = services[state.service].vets;
        const anyDetail = eligible.length === 1
          ? "Only Dr. Mary Major is qualified for this service."
          : "Your chosen time will identify the assigned vet.";

        content.innerHTML = `
          <fieldset>
            <legend>Vet preference (required)</legend>
            <div class="choices">
              ${choice("vet", "any", "Any available vet",
                        anyDetail, state.vet === "any")}
              ${Object.entries(vets).map(([name, vet]) => {
                const allowed = eligible.includes(name);
                return choice("vet", name, "Dr. " + name,
                  allowed ? "Works " + vet.schedule
                          : "Not qualified for this service",
                  state.vet === name, !allowed);
              }).join("")}
            </div>
          </fieldset>`;
      } else if (state.step === 2) {
        const slots = matchingSlots();
        content.innerHTML = `
          <p><strong>${dateLabel}</strong></p>
          <p class="hint">Clinic hours: 09:00–17:00.
             Closed for lunch: 12:00–13:00.</p>
          ${slots.length ? `
            <fieldset>
              <legend>Appointment time (required)</legend>
              <div class="choices">
                ${slots.map((slot, index) =>
                  choice("slot", index,
                    slot.start + "–" +
                    clock(minutes(slot.start) +
                          services[slot.service].minutes),
                    "Dr. " + slot.vet, state.slot === slot)
                ).join("")}
              </div>
            </fieldset>` : `
            <p role="status">
              No bookable times were returned for this selection
              on the demo Thursday.
            </p>
            <p class="hint">
              Only Thursday data is available here. The live app
              should offer other dates.
            </p>
            <button class="secondary" type="button" id="change-service">
              Change service
            </button>`}`;
      } else {
        content.innerHTML = summaryHTML() +
          (services[state.service].from
            ? `<p>A clinic-approved final estimate is required before
                 this service can be confirmed. None was supplied.</p>`
            : `<p>Check these details before confirming.
                 This is a demo booking.</p>`);
      }

      sync();
      if (moveFocus) title.focus();
    }

    content.addEventListener("change", event => {
      const input = event.target;
      if (!(input instanceof HTMLInputElement)) return;

      if (input.name === "service") {
        state.service = input.value;
        state.vet = "any";
        state.slot = null;
      } else if (input.name === "vet") {
        state.vet = input.value;
        state.slot = null;
      } else if (input.name === "slot") {
        state.slot = matchingSlots()[Number(input.value)] || null;
      }

      // Update the summary without replacing the focused radio.
      sync();
    });

    content.addEventListener("click", event => {
      if (event.target.closest("#change-service")) {
        state.step = 0;
        render(true);
      }
      if (event.target.closest("#restart")) {
        Object.assign(state, {
          step: 0, service: null, vet: "any", slot: null, done: false
        });
        render(true);
      }
    });

    back.addEventListener("click", () => {
      state.step--;
      render(true);
    });

    next.addEventListener("click", () => {
      if (next.disabled || state.done) return;

      if (state.step < 3) {
        state.step++;
        render(true);
        return;
      }

      const slot = state.slot;
      const stillMatches = slot && bookable(slot) &&
        slot.service === state.service &&
        (state.vet === "any" || slot.vet === state.vet);

      if (!stillMatches) {
        state.slot = null;
        state.step = 2;
        render(true);
        notice.textContent =
          "That time is no longer bookable. Please choose another time.";
        return;
      }

      if (services[state.service].from) return;

      // Production: atomically revalidate and create the booking on
      // the server; show success only after its successful response.
      state.done = true;
      render(true);
    });

    render();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

## 2. Design rationale

**Four separate steps, with a persistent summary.** At 375 px, each screen has one decision and a clear primary action. The fourth step reviews the booking before confirmation; success displays the same details. Back navigation preserves selections, while changing service or vet clears the dependent time selection.

**Fast paths for common services.** Wellness and vaccination appear first. “Any available vet” is the default preference, reducing unnecessary vet selection without skipping the required vet step. It means any **qualified** vet; choosing a time reveals the actual assigned clinician.

**Price transparency.** Prices appear on service cards, in the updating summary, and at review. Dental cleaning retains the exact **“from $280”** wording. A minimum is not a final charge: the prototype cannot confirm that service without a clinic-approved final estimate. Production should obtain that estimate and disclose mandatory fees before enabling confirmation.

**Necessary brand exception.** White text on `#7FD1AE` has approximately **1.9:1** contrast, failing AA for button labels. Primary buttons retain the mint background but use `color.ink`, approximately **7.7:1** contrast. Dark borders make controls distinguishable from white surfaces.

The prototype uses native radios, explicit labels, 48 px buttons, visible keyboard focus, logical focus movement, and polite summary announcements. Selection and unavailability are not communicated through colour alone. There are no fixed overlays or horizontal scrolling at 375 px. Production still needs keyboard, screen-reader, zoom, and device testing.

## 3. Data problems and handling

| Problem | Handling |
|---|---|
| Richard’s **10:00 exotic check-up** violates service eligibility. | Reject it. Only Mary may perform this service. The API should enforce the same capability rule. |
| Mary’s **11:30 dental cleaning** ends at **13:00**, crossing lunch. | Reject it. Validate the entire 90-minute interval, not just its start. |
| Richard’s **12:30 wellness exam** starts during lunch. | Reject it. No appointments may occupy the lunch interval. |
| Mary’s **16:45 wellness exam** ends at **17:15**, after closing. | Reject it. End time must be within clinic hours. |
| Only two entries survive validation. | Display **Mary: exotic check-up, 11:00–11:45** and **Richard: wellness exam, 14:00–14:30**, filtered by the selected service and vet preference. |
| No vaccination entries, and no valid dental entries. | Show a selection-specific empty state. Do not manufacture vaccination slots from wellness availability or interpret missing entries as permanent unavailability. Production should load other dates. |
| “Thursday” lacks an actual date and timezone. | Label the prototype’s date as illustrative. Production must return dated slots and the clinic’s timezone; recurring weekdays alone are insufficient. |
| Dental pricing is only a minimum. | Show the minimum clearly, but require an authoritative final estimate before committing. Clarify any additional mandatory charges. |
| Names and start times lack stable booking identifiers or freshness information. | Production should return slot/service/vet IDs and availability validity information. The server must atomically recheck eligibility, schedule, price, and availability when booking; a conflict returns the owner to time selection without discarding other choices. |

All supplied Thursday vet assignments meet their working-day rules. Client-side filtering protects this display, but the API must remain the booking authority.
